        'Pareto — if everyone prefers A to B, B should not win',
        'Independence of irrelevant alternatives — the ranking of A vs B should not change because a third option entered',
        'Everyone must vote strategically',
      ],
      answer: 3,
      why: 'Strategic manipulation is the subject of the sibling result — Gibbard and Satterthwaite proved every non-dictatorial system with 3+ options invites tactical voting. Arrow\'s four conditions (unrestricted domain, Pareto, IIA, non-dictatorship) are the ones that provably cannot coexist.',
    },
